;;; proactive.scm.example -- jobs the proactive plugin arms at session start.
;;;
;;; Copy to ~/.sah/proactive.scm (or <workspace>/.sah/proactive.scm) and edit.
;;; Each form is (kind ms text) or (kind name ms text):
;;;
;;;   every    repeat forever, first fire after MS
;;;   after    fire once, then the job is gone
;;;   note     like after, but only journals a line -- it never wakes the agent
;;;
;;; A text payload is delivered to the agent as its own turn, so keep these
;;; short and self-contained: the agent wakes with no idea what you were doing.

;; Look at the build every 5 minutes and fix it if it broke.
(every "build-watch" 300000
       "Run the build. If it is red, find the cause and fix it. If it is green, reply with just: green.")

;; Once, shortly after the session starts: pick up where the journal left off.
(after 5000
       "Summarize the open threads in this session and say which one you would continue.")

;; A pure journal marker: no turn, just a line the model sees later.
(note 60000 "checkpoint: an hour of work has gone by")
